0001>.\nConsider an extension\n<MATH_0003>\nas in the lemma. We can choose a sheaf of sets <MATH_0004>\nand a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0005>\nsuch that <MATH_0006>\nis surjective with kernel <MATH_0007>.\n(For example you can take any sheaf of sets surjecting\nonto <MATH_0008>.) Then\n<MATH_0009>\nSee Modules on Sites, Section <REF_0002>\nand in particular Lemma <REF_0003>.\nOf course <MATH_0010> determines a map\n<MATH_0011>\nwhich in turn determines a map\n<MATH_0012>\nwhich in turn determines the element of\n<MATH_0013>\ncorresponding to <MATH_0014> by the bijection of the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4f860822b77ca246d9e7212be73f6addb1f05ba2490a4d414b1ec20508fcbcc2", "unit_id": "tag:0GQ6:statement"}
